# A core whose save right after a load writes a field the load left
# stale: from frame 40 console 0's retro_serialize writes its state hash
# from a copy that each retro_run keeps and no load refreshes. A new process
# has no copy, so the from run passes; a load into the running session
# leaves the copy of frame 59, which a save before the next retro_run writes.
# error: console 0: a save right after the load differs at byte 12 from the state it loaded
console 0 core=test
console 1 core=test
option 0 link_test_mode stale_save
option 0 link_test_bad_frame 40
0 cable 0:0 1:0
30 save mid
60 end
